**Explanation of the UI flow**

| Step | What the user clicks | What the server does |
|------|----------------------|----------------------|
| **1 – Join queue** | **Join queue** button → `POST /queue/join` | Token is put at the end of `queue`. |
| **2 – Wait** | The page shows “Position N”. | No lock is granted yet. |
| **3 – Become first** | When the previous uploader presses **Finish upload**, the lock is released and the server pops the first waiting token. |
| **4 – Start upload** | **Start upload** button → `POST /queue/start`. If the user is first in line, the exclusive `upload_lock` is acquired and the token is stored as `session["lock_owner"]`. | The lock is now held; Dropzone becomes active because the page reload shows “You own the lock”. |
| **5 – Upload** | Dropzone automatically posts chunks to `/upload`. The server verifies `is_lock_owner(token)` before accepting any chunk. | Chunks are appended to a file on disk; after the last chunk the file is registered in `UPLOADS`. |
| **6 – Finish** | **Finish upload** button → `POST /queue/finish`. | The lock is released; the next waiting user can now call `/queue/start`. |
| **7 – Download** | The list under *Your uploaded file* is built from `/files`. Clicking the link hits `/download/<token>` which streams the file **only** if the token matches the current session. |

