Open <http://localhost:5000> in multiple browser windows (or incognito tabs) to see the queue in action.  

When one user clicks **Start upload**, Dropzone becomes active; the other user will see “You are in the queue – position 2”.  After the first user presses **Finish upload**, the lock is released and the second user can start his upload.

---

**Bottom line**

*The code now guarantees that only one upload proceeds at a time, that uploads are queued, and that files can be downloaded only by their owner.  The added checks (allowed extensions, size verification, CSRF awareness, per‑session tokens) close the most glaring security gaps of the original prototype.  For a production system replace the in‑memory structures with a persistent broker, plug in real authentication, enforce quotas and rate‑limits, and move the storage location outside the public webroot.*

