**Proof.**  
The heap is a *min‑heap* keyed by `ti`.  
`pop_min` always returns the element with the smallest key.
All stations that have been passed are inserted into the heap exactly
once and are removed only when they are used.
Therefore the popped station is the cheapest unused passed station. ∎



##### Lemma 2  
If at some moment the algorithm cannot reach the next station/destination,
then *any* feasible dive (i.e. any sequence of stations that allows Percy to
continue) must also use at least one of the stations currently stored in
the heap.

