It is deliberately kept simple so that you can read, compile, and run it on any POSIX‑compatible system (Linux, macOS, *BSD) or on Windows with a C compiler such as MSVC or MinGW.

I have also added **security‑focused commentary** and a few optional hardening steps (file‑level encryption, input validation, safe‑type handling, etc.) so you can see how a security researcher would think about hardening a tiny utility like this.

