**Solution Explanation**

For every quiz category we receive a line that contains the answers of the team.
The line may contain blanks – they have to be ignored – and three special
characters  

* `o` – correct answer, gives points  
* `x` – wrong answer, gives **0** points  
* `-` – skipped, gives **0** points  

In one (and only one) category the team may use a *joker* – the character
`$`. The first `$` that appears in the whole input is the *real* joker,
all the other `$` symbols are just ignored.  
The joker doubles the points earned in the category where it appears.
If no `$` appears, the points of the **last** category are doubled.

The first *boundary*‑1 questions of every category are worth **1** point,
the questions with index `≥ boundary` are worth **2** points.
`boundary` (the first question that is worth 2 points) is given in the first
line of the input.

The program has to

* print, for every category, the answer string **without blanks and without
  any `$`** (exactly the format shown in the examples);
* compute the total number of points earned;
* compute the number of points earned **at halftime** – the sum of the
  points of the first `ceil(N/2)` categories, where `N` is the number of
  categories;
* print the halftime points and the total points.

--------------------------------------------------------------------

#### Algorithm
```
read boundary
categories = empty list
joker_used = false
joker_category = -1                // index of the category that really has a joker

while a line can be read (until EOF)
        answer_string = ""         // characters that will be printed
        points = 0
        question_no = 1            // position inside the current category

        for each character ch in the line
                if ch is a blank            continue
                if ch == '$'
                        if !joker_used
                                joker_used = true
                                joker_category = index of current category
                        // the $ is never part of the printed answer
                        continue
                // ch is one of o, x, -
                answer_string += ch

                if ch == 'o'                         // correct answer
                        if question_no < boundary
                                points += 1          // 1‑point question
                        else
                                points += 2          // 2‑point question
                // x and - give 0 points
                question_no++
        end for

        store (answer_string, points) in categories list
end while

// --- apply joker ----------------------------------------------------
if joker_used               // a real $ was found
        categories[joker_category].points *= 2
else                        // no joker – double the last category
        categories.back().points *= 2

// --- compute totals --------------------------------------------------
total_points = sum of points of all categories
half_cnt   = ( number_of_categories + 1 ) / 2      // ceil(N/2)
halftime_points = sum of points of the first half_cnt categories

// --- output ---------------------------------------------------------
for each stored category in order
        print its answer_string
print halftime_points, a single space, total_points
```

