### Security‑researcher notes (Version A)

| Issue | Why it matters | Mitigation in the code |
|-------|----------------|------------------------|
| **Global mutable state** | Any other translation unit can modify `g_numbers` or `g_count`, potentially injecting malicious values. | Keep the globals `static` (file‑scope) so they are not visible outside this compilation unit. |
| **Bounded storage (`MAX_ELEMS`)** | Without a hard limit an attacker could overflow the array (stack/heap overflow). | The demo checks `n > MAX_ELEMS` before copying. In production you would also validate every write to the array. |
