##### Lemma 1  
After step&nbsp;2 (`appendTail`) the linked list contains *all* correctly read
integers, in the same order as they appear in the input.

**Proof.**  
The algorithm processes the tokens sequentially.  
For each token that is a correct integer it creates a new node and links it
after the current `tail`.  
`tail` is then updated to point to the new node.  
Thus each newly created node becomes the last element of the list, preserving
the input order. ∎



