The loop iterates over the original list from the original head to `NULL`.
During each iteration the current node’s `next` pointer is changed to point to
the previously processed node (`prev`).  
Consequently after processing the *k*-th node the first *k* nodes are linked
in reverse order.  
When the loop finishes (`cur == NULL`) all links are reversed and `prev`
points to the original last node, which becomes the new head.  
No node is created or destroyed, only their `next` pointers are altered,
hence the node set is unchanged. ∎



##### Lemma 3  
If the list is non‑empty, after step&nbsp;5 the program outputs the numbers in
