### 2.3 JSON Deserialization – The Common “Jackson” Pitfalls

| Vulnerability | Situation | Mitigation |
|---------------|-----------|------------|
| **Polymorphic Type Handling (CVE‑2020‑36518)** | `ObjectMapper.enableDefaultTyping()` makes attackers supply `@class` to instantiate arbitrary types (e.g., `javax.script.ScriptEngineManager`) | **Never enable default typing**. Use **`ObjectMapper.activateDefaultTyping` with a restrictive `PolymorphicTypeValidator`** (e.g., `BasicPolymorphicTypeValidator.builder().allowIfBaseType("com.myapp.dto").build()`). |
| **Deserialization of unknown fields** | Excess fields leak internal data structures (information disclosure) | `mapper.configure(DeserializationFeature.FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES, true);` |
