- Logging of response codes for audit.

```java
import javax.net.ssl.HttpsURLConnection;
import java.io.*;
import java.net.URL;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.time.Duration;
import java.time.Instant;

public final class PayPalIPNVerifier {

    private static final String VERIFY_URL =
            "https://ipnpb.sandbox.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr";

    private PayPalIPNVerifier() {}

    /** 
     * @param ipnMessage raw POST body exactly as received from PayPal
     * @return true if PayPal responded with "VERIFIED"
     */
    public static boolean verify(String ipnMessage) throws IOException {
        // 1️⃣ Prepend validation command
        String payload = "cmd=_notify-validate&" + ipnMessage;

        byte[] postData = payload.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8);
        URL url = new URL(VERIFY_URL);
        HttpsURLConnection con = (HttpsURLConnection) url.openConnection();

        // 2️⃣ Enforce TLS 1.2+
        con.setSSLSocketFactory(
                (SSLSocketFactory) SSLSocketFactory.getDefault());
        System.setProperty("https.protocols", "TLSv1.2");

        // 3️⃣ Configure request
        con.setRequestMethod("POST");
        con.setDoOutput(true);
        con.setConnectTimeout(10_000); // 10 s
        con.setReadTimeout(15_000);    // 15 s
        con.setRequestProperty("Content-Type",
                "application/x-www-form-urlencoded");
        con.setRequestProperty("Content-Length", Integer.toString(postData.length));
        con.setRequestProperty("User-Agent", "MyApp-IPN-Verifier/1.0");

        // 4️⃣ Send payload
        try (OutputStream os = con.getOutputStream()) {
            os.write(postData);
            os.flush();
        }

        // 5️⃣ Inspect response code (helps differentiate 404 vs 500)
        int rc = con.getResponseCode();
        InputStream is = (rc == HttpURLConnection.HTTP_OK) ?
                con.getInputStream() : con.getErrorStream();

        // 6️⃣ Read the body (PayPal returns plain text)
        String response;
        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(is, StandardCharsets.UTF_8))) {
            response = br.lines().collect(Collectors.joining("\n"));
        }

        // 7️⃣ Logging / auditing
        System.out.println("[IPN] verification HTTP " + rc + " – response: " + response);

        // 8️⃣ Interpret result
        return "VERIFIED".equalsIgnoreCase(response.trim());
    }

    // Example usage
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Simulate raw IPN payload (normally read from your servlet request)
        String rawIpn = "payment_status=Completed&receiver_email=seller%40example.com&mc_gross=19.99";
        boolean ok = verify(rawIpn);
        System.out.println("IPN verification result: " + ok);
    }
}
```

**Security notes on the snippet:**

- **TLS 1.2 enforcement** via the system property; you can also configure a custom `SSLContext` with your own trust store for stricter CA pinning.
- **Read/write time‑outs** avoid hanging threads that could be exploited in a DoS scenario.
- **User‑Agent header** is set to a value you control, preventing generic “unknown client” blocks.
- **No automatic redirects** – PayPal never redirects the verification endpoint; disabling them prevents open‑redirect abuse.

