Below is a **complete, end‑to‑end example** (with a few helper classes) that does what you asked for:

1. **Detects every local drive** (Windows `C:\`, `D:\` … or Unix root `/` etc.)  
2. **Recursively walks every directory** and builds an **index** (`Map<String,FileMeta>`) that stores only the information you need for a later search (path, size, last‑modified time, maybe a hash).  
3. **Serialises the index to disk** (JSON – easy to inspect, portable, and not memory‑hungry).  
4. **Searches the persisted index** without rescanning the file‑system.  
5. **Keeps the index up‑to‑date** by using the **NIO WatchService** to monitor every directory for create/modify/delete events and apply the delta to the persisted index.

> **⚠️ Security / Production notes**  
> * Running a full‑drive scan and a recursive `WatchService` can be **expensive** – the code uses a bounded thread‑pool and a “skip‑hidden‑system‑files” predicate to stay sane.  
> * On Windows the native `WatchService` can miss events on deeply nested trees; a production‑grade solution would fall back to a native library (e.g. JNA‑based `ReadDirectoryChangesW`).  
> * The index file must be stored **outside** any directory that is being watched (or you’ll get a “self‑update” loop).  
> * Handle **permission errors** gracefully – the code logs and continues rather than aborting.  

---

## 1. Project layout (single‑file for brevity)

```
src/
 └─ Main.java                 ← entry point
    DriveScanner.java         ← enumerate roots
    FileIndexer.java          ← build & persist index
    FileMeta.java             ← POJO for a file entry
    IndexStore.java           ← load / save JSON index
    FileSearcher.java         ← query the index
    FileWatcherService.java   ← recursive WatchService
    Utils.java                ← misc helpers
```

All classes are presented inline; you can copy‑paste them into a single `Main.java` file (they are package‑private static inner classes) or split them into separate files – the logic stays the same.

---

## 2. The code

```java
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Main.java   (package‑free example, Java 17+)
// ------------------------------------------------------------
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.nio.file.attribute.BasicFileAttributes;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;
import java.util.stream.*;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.core.*;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.*;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.module.*;

public class Main {
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Entry point – build (or load) the index, start watching, allow search
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 1️⃣  Detect all roots (drives on Windows, / on *nix)
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        List<Path> roots = DriveScanner.getRoots();
        System.out.println("Found drives: " + roots);

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 2️⃣  Load an existing index if present, otherwise build a fresh one
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        Path indexFile = Paths.get("file-index.json");   // <-- change as needed
        IndexStore store = new IndexStore(indexFile);
        Map<String, FileMeta> index = store.loadIfExists()
                .orElseGet(() -> {
                    System.out.println("No existing index – scanning all drives...");
                    return FileIndexer.buildIndex(roots);
                });

        // Persist the (just‑created) index – subsequent runs will load it instantly
        store.save(index);
        System.out.println("Index size: " + index.size() + " entries");

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 3️⃣  Start the background watcher that will keep the index fresh
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        FileWatcherService watcher = new FileWatcherService(roots, index, store);
        watcher.start();       // runs in its own daemon threads

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 4️⃣  Simple console REPL for searching the index
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        try (Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in)) {
            System.out.println("\n--- File‑search REPL (type 'exit' to quit) ---");
            while (true) {
                System.out.print("search> ");
                String line = in.nextLine();
                if (line == null || line.trim().equalsIgnoreCase("exit")) break;
                List<FileMeta> hits = FileSearcher.search(index, line.trim());
                System.out.println("Found " + hits.size() + " file(s):");
                hits.forEach(f -> System.out.println("  " + f.path));
            }
        }

        // shut down cleanly (watcher uses daemon threads, so JVM would exit anyway)
        watcher.stop();
        System.out.println("Bye!");
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 1️⃣  DriveScanner – list all the system’s root paths
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    static class DriveScanner {
        static List<Path> getRoots() {
            File[] roots = File.listRoots();
            if (roots == null) return List.of();
            return Arrays.stream(roots)
                    .map(File::toPath)
                    .collect(Collectors.toList());
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 2️⃣  FileMeta – what we store for each file in the index
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    static class FileMeta {
        public String path;          // absolute path (String is JSON‑friendly)
        public long size;
        public long lastModified;    // epoch‑millis
        // Optional: add hash, owner, permissions, etc.

        // Jackson needs a no‑arg ctor
        public FileMeta() {}

        public FileMeta(Path p, long size, long lastModified) {
            this.path = p.toString();
            this.size = size;
            this.lastModified = lastModified;
        }

        @Override
        public String toString() {
            return String.format("%s (size=%d, mtime=%s)",
                    path, size, Instant.ofEpochMilli(lastModified));
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 3️⃣  FileIndexer – walk the file‑system and build the map
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    static class FileIndexer {
        private static final Logger LOG = Logger.getLogger(FileIndexer.class.getName());
        private static final int MAX_THREADS = Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors() * 2;

        static Map<String, FileMeta> buildIndex(List<Path> roots) {
            ConcurrentMap<String, FileMeta> index = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
            ExecutorService exec = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(MAX_THREADS);

            try {
                List<Future<?>> futures = new ArrayList<>();
                for (Path root : roots) {
                    futures.add(exec.submit(() -> walkRoot(root, index)));
                }
                // wait for all to finish (propagate any exception)
                for (Future<?> f : futures) {
                    f.get();
                }
            } catch (Exception e) {
                LOG.log(Level.SEVERE, "Error while indexing", e);
            } finally {
                exec.shutdownNow();
            }
            return index;
        }

        /** Recursively walk a root and put entries into the shared ConcurrentMap */
        private static void walkRoot(Path root, ConcurrentMap<String, FileMeta> index) {
            try {
                Files.walkFileTree(root, EnumSet.of(FileVisitOption.FOLLOW_LINKS),
                        Integer.MAX_VALUE,
                        new SimpleFileVisitor<Path>() {
                            @Override
                            public FileVisitResult visitFile(Path file, BasicFileAttributes attrs) {
                                if (attrs.isRegularFile()) {
                                    index.put(file.toString(),
                                            new FileMeta(file, attrs.size(), attrs.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()));
                                }
                                return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                            }

                            @Override
                            public FileVisitResult visitFileFailed(Path file, IOException exc) {
                                // Silently ignore permission errors, log for diagnostics
                                LOG.log(Level.FINE, "Cannot access " + file + ": " + exc.getMessage());
                                return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                            }
                        });
            } catch (IOException e) {
                LOG.log(Level.WARNING, "Failed walking root " + root, e);
            }
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 4️⃣  IndexStore – JSON persistence of the map (Jackson)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    static class IndexStore {
        private final Path file;
        private final ObjectMapper mapper;

        IndexStore(Path file) {
            this.file = file;
            this.mapper = new ObjectMapper();
            // Use a custom serializer for the ConcurrentMap key type (String) → default works
            // but we enable pretty printing for human readability.
            mapper.enable(SerializationFeature.INDENT_OUTPUT);
        }

        /** Load from disk if the file exists, otherwise return empty */
        Optional<Map<String, FileMeta>> loadIfExists() {
            if (!Files.isRegularFile(file)) return Optional.empty();
            try (InputStream in = Files.newInputStream(file)) {
                JavaType type = mapper.getTypeFactory()
                        .constructMapType(HashMap.class, String.class, FileMeta.class);
                Map<String, FileMeta> map = mapper.readValue(in, type);
                return Optional.of(map);
            } catch (IOException e) {
                System.err.println("Failed loading index – will rebuild: " + e.getMessage());
                return Optional.empty();
            }
        }

        /** Overwrite the on‑disk file with the current map (atomic replace) */
        synchronized void save(Map<String, FileMeta> index) {
            try {
                Path tmp = Files.createTempFile("file-index", ".json");
                try (OutputStream out = Files.newOutputStream(tmp, StandardOpenOption.CREATE,
                        StandardOpenOption.TRUNCATE_EXISTING)) {
                    mapper.writeValue(out, index);
                }
                // atomic move into place (POSIX rename, Windows MoveFileEx)
                Files.move(tmp, file, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING, StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE);
                System.out.println("Persisted index (" + index.size() + " entries) to " + file);
            } catch (IOException e) {
                System.err.println("Failed persisting index: " + e.getMessage());
            }
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 5️⃣  FileSearcher – simple substring match (case‑insensitive)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    static class FileSearcher {
        /** Return a list of FileMeta whose path contains the query string */
        static List<FileMeta> search(Map<String, FileMeta> idx, String query) {
            if (query == null || query.isBlank()) return List.of();
            String q = query.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
            return idx.values().stream()
                    .filter(f -> f.path.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT).contains(q))
                    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(f -> f.path))
                    .collect(Collectors.toList());
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 6️⃣  FileWatcherService – watches *every* directory for changes
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    static class FileWatcherService {
        private static final Logger LOG = Logger.getLogger(FileWatcherService.class.getName());

        private final List<Path> roots;
        private final Map<String, FileMeta> index;   // mutable reference shared with main
        private final IndexStore store;
        private final ExecutorService executor;
        private WatchService watchService;
        private volatile boolean running = false;

        FileWatcherService(List<Path> roots,
                           Map<String, FileMeta> index,
                           IndexStore store) {
            this.roots = roots;
            this.index = index;
            this.store = store;
            this.executor = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor(r -> {
                Thread t = new Thread(r, "Watcher‑Thread");
                t.setDaemon(true);
                return t;
            });
        }

        /** Start the background thread that registers all dirs and processes events */
        void start() throws IOException {
            if (running) return;
            watchService = FileSystems.getDefault().newWatchService();
            registerAllRoots();
            running = true;
            executor.submit(this::processEvents);
        }

        /** Stop the background thread and close resources */
        void stop() {
            running = false;
            try {
                watchService.close();
            } catch (IOException ignored) {}
            executor.shutdownNow();
        }

        /** Register every directory under the supplied roots */
        private void registerAllRoots() throws IOException {
            for (Path root : roots) {
                Files.walkFileTree(root, new SimpleFileVisitor<>() {
                    @Override
                    public FileVisitResult preVisitDirectory(Path dir, BasicFileAttributes attrs) throws IOException {
                        // skip special system dirs that can cause infinite loops (e.g. Windows recycle bin)
                        if (shouldSkip(dir)) return FileVisitResult.SKIP_SUBTREE;
                        register(dir);
                        return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                    }
                });
            }
        }

        /** Helper – registers a single directory with the watch service */
        private void register(Path dir) throws IOException {
            dir.register(watchService,
                    new WatchEvent.Kind[]{StandardWatchEventKinds.ENTRY_CREATE,
                                          StandardWatchEventKinds.ENTRY_DELETE,
                                          StandardWatchEventKinds.ENTRY_MODIFY},
                    // high‑sensitivity on Windows (if supported)
                    SensitivityWatchEventModifier.HIGH);
        }

        /** Main loop – pulls events, updates the in‑memory index, side‑writes every N seconds */
        private void processEvents() {
            final long FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS = 30_000; // persist every 30 s (or after N events)
            long lastFlush = System.currentTimeMillis();

            while (running) {
                WatchKey key;
                try {
                    // block up to 10 s so we can flush periodically even if idle
                    key = watchService.poll(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                    break;
                } catch (ClosedWatchServiceException cwse) {
                    break;  // service stopped
                }

                if (key == null) { // timeout – maybe flush
                    if (System.currentTimeMillis() - lastFlush > FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS) {
                        store.save(index);
                        lastFlush = System.currentTimeMillis();
                    }
                    continue;
                }

                Path dir = (Path) key.watchable();

                for (WatchEvent<?> ev : key.pollEvents()) {
                    WatchEvent.Kind<?> kind = ev.kind();

                    // Overflow means we missed events; safest is to re‑scan the whole dir
                    if (kind == StandardWatchEventKinds.OVERFLOW) {
                        LOG.warning("Overflow detected – rescanning " + dir);
                        rescanDirectory(dir);
                        continue;
                    }

                    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
                    WatchEvent<Path> pathEvent = (WatchEvent<Path>) ev;
                    Path child = dir.resolve(pathEvent.context());

                    // ---------------------------------------------------------
                    // 1️⃣  CREATE  – if directory, register it recursively; if file, add to index
                    // ---------------------------------------------------------
                    if (kind == StandardWatchEventKinds.ENTRY_CREATE) {
                        try {
                            if (Files.isDirectory(child, LinkOption.NOFOLLOW_LINKS)) {
                                registerAllUnder(child); // recursion
                            } else if (Files.isRegularFile(child, LinkOption.NOFOLLOW_LINKS)) {
                                BasicFileAttributes a = Files.readAttributes(child, BasicFileAttributes.class);
                                index.put(child.toString(), new FileMeta(child, a.size(), a.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()));
                            }
                        } catch (IOException ioe) {
                            LOG.fine("Create event ignored – cannot access " + child + ": " + ioe);
                        }
                    }

                    // ---------------------------------------------------------
                    // 2️⃣  MODIFY – update size/mtime if it's a regular file
                    // ---------------------------------------------------------
                    else if (kind == StandardWatchEventKinds.ENTRY_MODIFY) {
                        if (Files.isRegularFile(child, LinkOption.NOFOLLOW_LINKS)) {
                            try {
                                BasicFileAttributes a = Files.readAttributes(child, BasicFileAttributes.class);
                                index.put(child.toString(),
                                        new FileMeta(child, a.size(), a.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()));
                            } catch (IOException ioe) {
                                LOG.fine("Modify ignored – cannot read attrs of " + child + ": " + ioe);
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    // ---------------------------------------------------------
                    // 3️⃣  DELETE – remove from index, also clean up any sub‑entries if a dir was removed
                    // ---------------------------------------------------------
                    else if (kind == StandardWatchEventKinds.ENTRY_DELETE) {
                        // if it's a directory we need to bulk‑remove all children
                        // (the key may have already been cancelled, but that's fine)
                        String prefix = child.toString() + File.separator;
                        index.keySet().removeIf(p -> p.equals(child.toString()) || p.startsWith(prefix));
                    }
                }

                // Reset the key – if it’s no longer valid the directory was removed
                boolean valid = key.reset();
                if (!valid) {
                    LOG.fine("WatchKey no longer valid (dir deleted?): " + dir);
                }

                // Periodic flush
                if (System.currentTimeMillis() - lastFlush > FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS) {
                    store.save(index);
                    lastFlush = System.currentTimeMillis();
                }
            }

            // final flush on shutdown
            store.save(index);
            LOG.info("Watcher thread terminating – final index persisted.");
        }

        /** Register a tree of directories under 'start' – similar to registerAllRoots() but for a new subtree */
        private void registerAllUnder(Path start) throws IOException {
            Files.walkFileTree(start, new SimpleFileVisitor<>() {
                @Override
                public FileVisitResult preVisitDirectory(Path dir, BasicFileAttributes attrs) throws IOException {
                    if (shouldSkip(dir)) return FileVisitResult.SKIP_SUBTREE;
                    register(dir);
                    return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                }

                @Override
                public FileVisitResult visitFile(Path file, BasicFileAttributes attrs) throws IOException {
                    if (attrs.isRegularFile()) {
                        index.put(file.toString(),
                                new FileMeta(file, attrs.size(), attrs.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()));
                    }
                    return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                }
            });
        }

        /** Re‑scan a directory fully (used when overflow occurs) */
        private void rescanDirectory(Path dir) {
            try {
                // remove any stale entries first
                String prefix = dir.toString() + File.separator;
                index.keySet().removeIf(p -> p.startsWith(prefix));

                // then walk and add fresh
                registerAllUnder(dir);
            } catch (IOException e) {
                LOG.warning("Failed re‑scanning " + dir + ": " + e);
            }
        }

        /** Simple heuristic to avoid watching things that would cause loops or are irrelevant */
        private static boolean shouldSkip(Path p) {
            String name = p.getFileName().toString().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
