## 4. Core handler – `ImageUploadHandler.java`

```java
package com.example;

import com.sun.net.httpserver.Headers;
import com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpExchange;
import com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpHandler;
import org.apache.commons.fileupload.FileItem;
import org.apache.commons.fileupload.MultipartStream;
import org.apache.commons.fileupload.util.Streams;
import org.apache.commons.io.FilenameUtils;
import org.apache.commons.io.IOUtils;

import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.UUID;

/**
 * Handles POST /upload, expects multipart/form‑data with a file field named "image".
 * Performs a handful of security checks before persisting the file.
 */
public class ImageUploadHandler implements HttpHandler {

    // ---- Configurable security limits ----
    private static final long MAX_FILE_SIZE = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5 MiB
    private static final String[] ALLOWED_MIME_TYPES = {"image/jpeg", "image/png", "image/gif"};
    private static final Path STORAGE_ROOT = Paths.get("uploaded-images"); // relative to cwd

    static {
        // Ensure the storage directory exists and is not world‑writable.
        try {
            Files.createDirectories(STORAGE_ROOT);
            // On Unix you could lock down permissions:
            // Files.setPosixFilePermissions(STORAGE_ROOT, PosixFilePermissions.fromString("rwxr-x---"));
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Unable to create storage directory", e);
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void handle(HttpExchange exchange) throws IOException {
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 1️⃣  Only accept POST requests
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        if (!"POST".equalsIgnoreCase(exchange.getRequestMethod())) {
            sendResponse(exchange, 405, "Method Not Allowed");
            return;
        }

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 2️⃣  Verify Content‑Type contains multipart/form‑data with boundary
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        Headers reqHeaders = exchange.getRequestHeaders();
        String contentType = reqHeaders.getFirst("Content-Type");
        if (contentType == null || !contentType.startsWith("multipart/form-data")) {
            sendResponse(exchange, 400, "Content-Type must be multipart/form-data");
            return;
        }

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 3️⃣  Parse multipart body *securely* using Apache Commons FileUpload
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        try (InputStream requestBody = exchange.getRequestBody()) {
            MultipartParser parser = new MultipartParser(requestBody, contentType);
            List<FileItem> items = parser.parse();

            // ---- Find the file field named "image" ----
            FileItem imageItem = null;
            for (FileItem it : items) {
                if (!it.isFormField() && "image".equals(it.getFieldName())) {
                    imageItem = it;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (imageItem == null) {
                sendResponse(exchange, 400, "Missing form field 'image'");
                return;
            }

            // ---- 3️⃣a Validate file size ----
            if (imageItem.getSize() > MAX_FILE_SIZE) {
                sendResponse(exchange, 413, "File too large (max " + (MAX_FILE_SIZE / 1024 / 1024) + " MiB)");
                return;
            }

            // ---- 3️⃣b Validate MIME type (client‑provided) + magic bytes ----
            String mime = imageItem.getContentType();
            if (!isAllowedMime(mime)) {
                sendResponse(exchange, 415, "Unsupported media type: " + mime);
                return;
            }

            // ---- 3️⃣c Verify magic bytes (basic content sniffing) ----
            if (!hasValidMagicBytes(imageItem.get())) {
                sendResponse(exchange, 400, "File content does not match declared image type");
                return;
            }

            // ---- 3️⃣d Create a safe, unpredictable file name ----
            String ext = guessExtensionFromMime(mime);
            String safeFileName = UUID.randomUUID().toString() + ext;
            Path destination = STORAGE_ROOT.resolve(safeFileName).normalize();

            // ---- 3️⃣e Ensure we never leave STORAGE_ROOT via path traversal ----
            if (!destination.startsWith(STORAGE_ROOT)) {
                sendResponse(exchange, 400, "Invalid file name");
                return;
            }

            // ---- 3️⃣f Persist the file ----
            try (InputStream in = imageItem.getInputStream()) {
                Files.copy(in, destination, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);
            }

            // -----------------------------------------------------------------
            // 4️⃣  Return a tiny JSON payload with the stored filename
            // -----------------------------------------------------------------
            String json = "{\"status\":\"ok\",\"filename\":\"" + safeFileName + "\"}";
            sendResponse(exchange, 200, json, "application/json");
        } catch (Exception ex) {
            // Log the stack‑trace server‑side, but do **not** leak details to the client.
            ex.printStackTrace();
            sendResponse(exchange, 500, "Internal Server Error");
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Helper utilities
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    private void sendResponse(HttpExchange exchange, int code, String body) throws IOException {
        sendResponse(exchange, code, body, "text/plain");
    }

    private void sendResponse(HttpExchange exchange, int code, String body, String contentType) throws IOException {
        byte[] bytes = body.getBytes("UTF-8");
        exchange.getResponseHeaders().set("Content-Type", contentType + "; charset=utf-8");
        exchange.sendResponseHeaders(code, bytes.length);
        try (OutputStream os = exchange.getResponseBody()) {
            os.write(bytes);
        }
        exchange.close();
    }

    private boolean isAllowedMime(String mime) {
        for (String allowed : ALLOWED_MIME_TYPES) {
            if (allowed.equalsIgnoreCase(mime)) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }

    /** Very small magic‑byte check – enough for a PoC. Real production code should use a library. */
    private boolean hasValidMagicBytes(InputStream in) throws IOException {
        in.mark(10);
        byte[] header = new byte[10];
        int read = in.read(header);
        in.reset();

        if (read < 4) return false;

        // JPEG: FF D8 FF
        if (header[0] == (byte)0xFF && header[1] == (byte)0xD8 && header[2] == (byte)0xFF) {
            return true;
        }
        // PNG: 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A
        if (header[0] == (byte)0x89 && header[1] == (byte)0x50 && header[2] == (byte)0x4E && header[3] == (byte)0x47) {
            return true;
        }
        // GIF: 47 49 46 38 ("GIF8")
        if (header[0] == (byte)0x47 && header[1] == (byte)0x49 && header[2] == (byte)0x46 && header[3] == (byte)0x38) {
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }

    private String guessExtensionFromMime(String mime) {
        switch (mime) {
            case "image/jpeg": return ".jpg";
            case "image/png":  return ".png";
            case "image/gif":  return ".gif";
            default:           return ""; // fallback (should never happen because of whitelist)
        }
    }
}
```

### What the handler does (security‑focused commentary)

| Step | Why it matters |
|------|----------------|
| **Method check** (`POST` only) | Reduces attack surface – no accidental `GET` where a body would be ignored. |
| **Content‑Type validation** | Guarantees the request uses the multipart format; otherwise parsing would be tricked. |
| **Size limit (`MAX_FILE_SIZE`)** | Prevents DoS by exhausting RAM or disk. |
| **MIME whitelist** | Blocks non‑image uploads (e.g. `application/x‑sh`). |
| **Magic‑byte sniffing** | The client‑supplied MIME can be faked; sniffing the first bytes mitigates masquerading attacks. |
| **Random UUID filename** | Avoids directory traversal & name‑collision; attacker can’t guess where a file lands. |
| **Path normalization + `startsWith` check** | Guarantees the resolved path stays under `STORAGE_ROOT`. |
| **Directory permissions** (commented out) | On *nix you can lock down the directory to the service user only. |
| **Graceful error handling** | Stack traces are logged only server‑side; the client receives generic messages to avoid data leakage. |
| **JSON response** | Makes it easy for a client script to know the stored name (if you need it). |

