## 7. Checklist for **production‑hardened** deployment

Below is a quick “security‑researcher” checklist you can copy‑paste into your own documentation.

| ✔️ Item | Rationale |
|--------|-----------|
| **Run as a non‑root, dedicated OS user** | Limits impact of a compromise. |
| **Bind to a specific interface** (`localhost` in the PoC) | Avoid exposure to the Internet unless you mean it. |
| **TLS (HTTPS)** | Prevents eavesdropping / MITM on the image payload. Use `com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpsConfigurator` or front‑end with Nginx/Apache. |
| **Rate‑limit per IP** | Mitigates DoS by bombarding the endpoint with many small requests. |
| **Antivirus / malware scanning** (ClamAV, etc.) | Detects steganography or malicious payloads hidden in images. |
| **Content‑type verification using a robust library** (e.g., `java-imageio` to attempt reading the image) | Guarantees the file is a parsable image. |
| **Quarantine & retention policy** | Delete old files after a configurable period. |
| **Logging & audit trails** (including source IP, timestamp, filename, size) | Helps forensic analysis if something goes wrong. |
| **CORS restrictions** (if accessed via browsers) | Set `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` to only permitted domains. |
| **Secure temp directory** (`DiskFileItemFactory.setRepository`) | Make sure temporary files cannot be read by other users. |
| **Code signing / integrity verification** (if distributing the jar) | Prevent tampering. |
| **Dependency vetting** (`mvn dependency:tree`, SBOM) | Ensure no vulnerable versions of Commons‑FileUpload/IO are used. |
| **Unit / integration tests for edge cases** | Fuzz the multipart parser to ensure no crashes or OOM. |
| **Static analysis (SpotBugs, OWASP Dependency‑Check)** | Flag any known weaknesses. |

