## 3. POJO – `Recording.java`

```java
package com.example.mouserecorder;

import java.awt.Point;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

/**
 * One logical mouse‑movement recording.
 * - name : user‑provided identifier (e.g. "test‑1")
 * - points : list of (x,y,timestamp) tuples.
 *   We use a custom PointWithTime because java.awt.Point holds only x,y.
 */
public class Recording {
    public String name;

    /** Each entry contains (x, y, timeSinceStartMillis). */
    public static class PointWithTime {
        public int x, y;
        public long time; // ms since start of recording

        public PointWithTime(int x, int y, long time) {
            this.x = x;
            this.y = y;
            this.time = time;
        }

        public Point toPoint() {
            return new Point(x, y);
        }
    }

    public List<PointWithTime> points = new ArrayList<>();

    public Recording() {}                         // needed for Gson
    public Recording(String name) { this.name = name; }

    /** Convenience for the GUI – show as "name (duration s)". */
    public long getDuration() {
        if (points.isEmpty()) return 0;
        return points.get(points.size() - 1).time;
    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return name + " (" + (getDuration() / 1000.0) + " s)";
    }
}
```

