| **Only TLS 1.3 ciphers appear** | TLS 1.3 suites are always (EC)DHE, but the JDK does not expose curve details via the `keyExchange` field. | For TLS 1.3 you can retrieve the curve via `SSLParameters.getSupportedGroups()` after the handshake, or use Bouncy Castle which exposes the `SupportedGroupExtension`. |
| **Large primes cause memory pressure** | Very large DH primes (≥4096 bits) may be printed partially to avoid huge console output. | Adjust the truncation length (`substring(0,…)`) or write to a file. |

