| ✅ Checklist item | Why it matters |
|-------------------|----------------|
| **Unique IV per encryption** | Re‑using the GCM nonce with the same key leaks the XOR of the plaintexts. The code above always generates a fresh 12‑byte random IV. |
| **Key storage** | The secret key must never reside on the tag. Keep it in a secure element, encrypted database, or derive it from a user secret (PBKDF2/Argon2). |
