## 2. Hibernate configuration (`src/main/resources/hibernate.cfg.xml`)

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE hibernate-configuration PUBLIC
        "-//Hibernate/Hibernate Configuration DTD 3.0//EN"
        "http://www.hibernate.org/dtd/hibernate-configuration-3.0.dtd">

<hibernate-configuration>
    <session-factory>
        <!-- ---------------------------------------------------
             H2 connection (file‑based for persistence across runs)
             --------------------------------------------------- -->
        <!--
            For maximum security in production you would NOT embed the
            password in the XML. Instead use environment variables,
            a secrets manager, or a JNDI datasource defined by the app server.
        -->
        <property name="hibernate.connection.driver_class">org.h2.Driver</property>

        <!--
            JDBC URL:
            - `~/testdb` puts the DB file into the user home (portable)
            - `DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1` keeps the DB alive for the JVM lifetime
            - `LOCK_TIMEOUT=10000` (10 s) prevents dead‑lock hangs
        -->
        <property name="hibernate.connection.url">
            jdbc:h2:file:~/testdb;DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1;LOCK_TIMEOUT=10000
        </property>

        <!-- The default H2 user/password is "sa"/blank; change for prod! -->
        <property name="hibernate.connection.username">sa</property>
        <property name="hibernate.connection.password"></property>

        <!-- ---------------------------------------------------
             Hibernate dialect & JDBC batch settings (performance)
             --------------------------------------------------- -->
        <property name="hibernate.dialect">org.hibernate.dialect.H2Dialect</property>

        <!-- Automatically create / update the schema. In production set to 'validate' -->
        <property name="hibernate.hbm2ddl.auto">update</property>

        <!-- Show SQL only for debugging (disable in production) -->
        <property name="hibernate.show_sql">false</property>
        <property name="hibernate.format_sql">true</property>

        <!-- ---------------------------------------------------
             Security‑hardening flags
             --------------------------------------------------- -->
        <!-- Force use of prepared statements – prevents SQL‑injection -->
        <property name="hibernate.jdbc.use_get_generated_keys">true</property>

        <!-- Disable the old Hibernate query cache that can leak data across users -->
        <property name="hibernate.cache.use_second_level_cache">false</property>
        <property name="hibernate.cache.use_query_cache">false</property>

        <!-- Enable JPA validation (Bean Validation) – rejects malformed data early -->
        <property name="javax.persistence.validation.mode">AUTO</property>

        <!-- ---------------------------------------------------
             Register your annotated entity classes
             --------------------------------------------------- -->
        <mapping class="com.example.model.Employee"/>
    </session-factory>
</hibernate-configuration>
```

### Why these settings are “secure”

| Setting | Reason |
|---------|--------|
| **Prepared statements (`use_get_generated_keys`)** | Guarantees that values are bound, not concatenated, eliminating classic SQL‑injection vectors. |
| **`hibernate.hbm2ddl.auto=update`** (dev) | Keeps the schema in sync without manual DDL. In production you should change this to **`validate`** or **`none`** to avoid accidental schema changes. |
| **`show_sql=false`** | Prevents accidental leakage of sensitive data (e.g., passwords) to the console or logs. |
| **Disabling second‑level & query cache** | Prevents accidental cross‑tenant data leakage when the same `SessionFactory` is shared among unrelated users. |
| **Bean Validation (`javax.persistence.validation.mode=AUTO`)** | Guarantees that `@NotNull`, `@Size`, etc., are enforced before anything reaches the DB. |

