## 6. Common Pitfalls & Debugging Tips

| Issue | Why it Happens | Fix |
|-------|----------------|-----|
| **`java.lang.NoClassDefFoundError: jdk/nashorn/api/scripting/NashornScriptEngineFactory`** | Running on a JDK > 15 where Nashorn was removed. | Use a JDK 8 (or 11 with Nashorn jar) for the client. The official 1.8.9 forge launches with a bundled JRE 8, so you’re safe if you use the standard launcher. |
| **`require` can’t find a module** | Path resolution is relative to the **current working directory**, not the script’s folder. | In the shim’s `require` implementation, resolve relative paths using `__dirname` (provided to each module by the wrapper). |
| **Java classes visible from JS (security risk)** | Engine started with default settings (`--no-java` not set). | Add `--no-java` flag or supply a custom `ClassFilter`. |
| **Node output gets garbled** | Both the Minecraft log and the Node stdout are writing to the same console. | Run Minecraft from a terminal (not a GUI launcher) or pipe logs to a file. The shim already prefixes Node lines with `[Node]`. |
| **Scripts freeze the game** | Long‑running scripts executed on the **main thread**. | Off‑load heavy JS computation to a separate Java thread (e.g., `ExecutorService`) and only interact with the game thread when needed (via `Minecraft.getMinecraft().addScheduledTask`). |

