Below is a **complete, ready‑to‑run Puppeteer script** that demonstrates how to automate a Stripe Checkout form that uses the classic “Elements” inputs (card number, expiry, CVC, etc.).  
The script shows:

* How to **handle the iframes** that Stripe injects for the card fields.  
* How to **type into the fields** using the correct selectors (`#cardNumber`, `#cardExpiry`, `#cardCvc`, `#billingName`).  
* How to **select a country** from the `<select id="billingCountry">` element.  
* How to **click the submit button** (`.SubmitButton`).  

> **⚠️ IMPORTANT**  
> *Never* run this script with real card details on a production site. Use Stripe’s test mode (test API keys) and Stripe‑provided test card numbers (e.g. `4242 4242 4242 4242`).  
> *Always* respect the target site’s terms of service, robots.txt, and obtain explicit permission before running automated browsers against it.

---

## 1️⃣ Prerequisites

| What you need | How to get it |
|---------------|---------------|
| **Node.js** (≥ 14) | <https://nodejs.org/> |
| **Puppeteer** (headless Chrome) | `npm i puppeteer` |
| (Optional) **dotenv** for environment variables | `npm i dotenv` |

Create a folder, run `npm init -y` and install the dependencies:

```bash
npm i puppeteer dotenv   # dotenv is optional, but handy for secrets
```

Create a file called `.env` (if you want to keep the card data out of source code):

```dotenv
CARD_NUMBER=4242424242424242
CARD_EXPIRY=12/34
CARD_CVC=123
CARD_HOLDER=John Doe
COUNTRY=US
```

---

## 2️⃣ The Script (`stripe-fill.js`)

```javascript
/**
 * stripe-fill.js
 * -------------------------
 * Automated fill‑in of a Stripe Checkout form using Puppeteer.
 *
 * This script showcases:
 *   • Handling Stripe Elements that live inside iframes.
 *   • Selecting a value from a <select>.
 *   • Clicking the final Submit button.
 *
 * NOTE: Use ONLY test data (Stripe test cards) and run this
 * against a test environment (e.g. a staging server or a local
 * copy of the checkout page). Do NOT use real card numbers.
 */

require('dotenv').config();   // <-- optional, for .env support

const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONFIGURATION – replace these values with your own test data if you
// aren't using a .env file.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------
const CONFIG = {
  // Target URL of the checkout page (must be reachable from the machine)
  checkoutUrl: 'https://your‑site.example.com/checkout', // <-- change!

  // Card details – use Stripe test values only.
  cardNumber: process.env.CARD_NUMBER || '4242424242424242',
  cardExpiry: process.env.CARD_EXPIRY || '12/34', // MM/YY
  cardCvc:    process.env.CARD_CVC    || '123',
  cardHolder:process.env.CARD_HOLDER|| 'John Doe',

  // Billing country – the <option> value attribute (ISO‑2 code, e.g. "US")
  country:    process.env.COUNTRY    || 'US',

  // Timeout / wait settings (ms)
  navigationTimeout: 30000,
  typingDelay: 80, // simulate human typing
};

(async () => {
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣ Launch browser
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const browser = await puppeteer.launch({
    headless: false,          // set true for headless CI runs
    defaultViewport: null,   // use full screen size
    args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-setuid-sandbox'],
  });

  const page = await browser.newPage();

  // Set a generous timeout for navigation / waiting
  page.setDefaultNavigationTimeout(CONFIG.navigationTimeout);
  page.setDefaultTimeout(CONFIG.navigationTimeout);

  console.log('➡️  Navigating to checkout page...');
  await page.goto(CONFIG.checkoutUrl, { waitUntil: 'networkidle2' });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣ Helper: get the iframe that hosts a given Stripe Element
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  /**
   * Stripe renders each field inside its own <iframe>.  The iframe can
   * be identified by the name attribute that contains the element id
   * we care about (e.g. "cardNumber", "cardExpiry", "cardCvc").
   *
   * @param {string} elementId  – the id attribute used on the placeholder div
   * @returns {Promise<Frame>}  – the puppeteer Frame object
   */
  async function getStripeIframe(elementId) {
    // Wait for the placeholder <div> that Stripe replaces with an iframe
    await page.waitForSelector(`#${elementId}`, { visible: true });

    // Find the iframe whose name contains the element id
    const frame = page
      .frames()
      .find(f => f.name().includes(elementId));
    if (!frame) {
      throw new Error(`❌ Unable to locate iframe for ${elementId}`);
    }
    return frame;
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 3️⃣ Fill the *Card Number* field
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  console.log('✍️  Filling Card Number...');
  const numberFrame = await getStripeIframe('cardNumber');
  const numberInput = await numberFrame.waitForSelector('input[name="cardnumber"]', { visible: true });
  await numberInput.type(CONFIG.cardNumber, { delay: CONFIG.typingDelay });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 4️⃣ Fill the *Expiry* field
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  console.log('✍️  Filling Expiry...');
  const expiryFrame = await getStripeIframe('cardExpiry');
  const expiryInput = await expiryFrame.waitForSelector('input[name="exp-date"]', { visible: true });
  await expiryInput.type(CONFIG.cardExpiry, { delay: CONFIG.typingDelay });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 5️⃣ Fill the *CVC* field
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  console.log('✍️  Filling CVC...');
  const cvcFrame = await getStripeIframe('cardCvc');
  const cvcInput = await cvcFrame.waitForSelector('input[name="cvc"]', { visible: true });
  await cvcInput.type(CONFIG.cardCvc, { delay: CONFIG.typingDelay });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 6️⃣ Fill the *Cardholder Name* (plain input – no iframe)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  console.log('✍️  Filling Cardholder Name...');
  await page.waitForSelector('#billingName', { visible: true });
  await page.type('#billingName', CONFIG.cardHolder, { delay: CONFIG.typingDelay });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 7️⃣ Select the *Country* from the <select>
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  console.log('🌍 Selecting Country...');
  await page.waitForSelector('#billingCountry', { visible: true });
  // The <option> values in Stripe are ISO‑2 country codes.
  await page.select('#billingCountry', CONFIG.country);

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 8️⃣ Click the *Pay* button (class .SubmitButton)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  console.log('🔘 Clicking the Submit button...');
  await page.waitForSelector('.SubmitButton', { visible: true });
  // Some Stripe implementations disable the button until the Elements are valid.
  // Using `click` followed by a short wait is usually enough.
  await page.click('.SubmitButton');

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 9️⃣ Wait for a post‑submission indicator (optional)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // Adjust this selector to something that appears only after a successful
  // payment (e.g. a success message, a redirect URL, etc.).
  try {
    await page.waitForNavigation({ waitUntil: 'networkidle2', timeout: 15000 });
    console.log('✅ Navigation after submit detected.');
  } catch (e) {
    console.warn('⚠️  No navigation detected – maybe a modal or SPA update.');
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 10️⃣ Close the browser (or keep it open for debugging)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // await browser.close();   // uncomment when you are done
})().catch(err => {
  console.error('❗  Script failed:', err);
  process.exit(1);
});
```

### How It Works – Step‑by‑Step Explanation

| Step | What the code does | Why it matters |
|------|-------------------|----------------|
| **1** | Launches a Chrome instance (headless‑off for visual debugging). | Gives you a controllable browser. |
| **2** | `getStripeIframe()` waits for the placeholder container (`#cardNumber`, `#cardExpiry`, `#cardCvc`) and then finds the associated iframe that Stripe creates. | Stripe Elements are **sandboxed inside iframes**; you cannot type directly into the outer DOM. |
| **3‑5** | Inside each iframe we locate the `<input>` element (`name="cardnumber"`, `name="exp-date"`, `name="cvc"`). | These are the real fields the user interacts with. |
| **6** | Types the cardholder name into `#billingName`. | This field is not an iframe, so a regular selector works. |
| **7** | `page.select('#billingCountry', CONFIG.country)` picks the `<option>` whose `value` matches the two‑letter ISO code. | Guarantees the correct country code is sent to Stripe. |
| **8** | Clicks the button with class `SubmitButton`. | Triggers Stripe’s tokenization and form submission. |
| **9** | Waits for navigation or any post‑submit change you care about. | Lets you verify success (or capture error messages). |
| **10** | Closes the browser (optional). | Clean exit. |

