It ships as a single module (`axiosClient.js`/`axiosClient.ts`) and can be imported anywhere in your component tree or inside custom hooks.

> **Why a “security‑researcher” version?**  
> • All network traffic is forced over HTTPS.  
> • Sensitive credentials are never stored in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`.  
> • JWTs are kept in memory (or a `httpOnly` cookie) and refreshed automatically.  
> • CSRF protection is built‑in when the backend uses double‑submit cookie technique.  
