## 3. Render the iframe in `profile.ejs`

Now that we always have the *raw* SoundCloud URL stored in `musician.soundcloud`, we just need to **build the embed URL inside the view**.

### 3.1. Add a small EJS helper

EJS lets you embed JavaScript directly. Put the helper at the top of the file (or, better, expose it from `app.locals` in `app.js` – see the “global helper” section at the bottom).

```ejs
<%
// Helper – same logic as the Node version, but tiny because we only need the src.
function soundcloudEmbedSrc(url) {
    if (!url) return '';
    const clean = url.split('?')[0].trim();         // strip UTM params
    const encoded = encodeURIComponent(clean);
    return `https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=${encoded}` +
           `&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false` +
           `&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false` +
           `&show_teaser=true&visual=true`;
}
%>
```

### 3.2. Use the helper inside the markup

Replace the old iframe line:

```ejs
<iframe width="100%" height="300" scrolling="no" frameborder="no"
        src="<%= musician.soundcloud %>"></iframe>
```

**with**

```ejs
<% if (musician.soundcloud && isValidSoundCloudUrl(musician.soundcloud)) { %>
    <iframe width="100%" height="300" scrolling="no" frameborder="no"
            allow="autoplay"
            src="<%= soundcloudEmbedSrc(musician.soundcloud) %>">
    </iframe>
<% } else { %>
    <p>No SoundCloud track linked.</p>
<% } %>
```

*(We keep the `allow="autoplay"` attribute for completeness.)*

