## 8️⃣ Checklist – What to Verify Before Going Live

| ✅ | Item |
|---|------|
| **Configuration** | All secrets read from env, validated, and not logged. |
| **CORS** | Only explicit origins allowed (or none if only internal). |
| **Headers** | Helmet enabled (`X‑Content‑Type‑Options`, `X‑Frame‑Options`, `Strict‑Transport‑Security`). |
| **Rate Limiting** | Applied globally or per‑endpoint for auth routes. |
| **Input Validation** | Every `POST/PUT/PATCH` has a Joi/Zod schema. |
| **Sanitisation** | Mongo‑sanitize middleware in place. |
| **Error Responses** | No stack traces, generic 500, specific 4xx for known errors. |
| **Logging** | Structured JSON, no PII, include request IDs (e.g., `cls-hooked` or `express-request-id`). |
| **Graceful Shutdown** | `SIGTERM` drains connections, closes DB, exits with 0. |
| **Health Endpoints** | `/healthz` reports DB & process status, ready for load‑balancer probes. |
| **Testing** | ≥80% coverage, CI runs on every commit. |
| **Dependency Scanning** | `npm audit` CI step passes, no high‑severity vulns. |
| **Container Hardening** | Non‑root user in Dockerfile, read‑only filesystem where possible. |
| **TLS** | Serve behind an HTTPS terminator (NGINX, Cloud Load Balancer). |

