## 6. Security‑Research Checklist (why this matters)

If you intend to **audit** or **penetration‑test** a similar system, consider checking:

| Area | Typical Findings |
|------|------------------|
| **Authentication** | Weak JWT secret, token leakage, missing expiration, no token revocation. |
| **Password storage** | Low bcrypt rounds, plain‑text storage, predictable salts. |
| **Input validation** | No schema enforcement → NoSQL injection (`{ "$gt": "" }`), JSON injection, massive payloads. |
| **Socket.io** | Event name enumeration, unauthenticated socket connections, lack of rate limiting. |
| **Game logic** | Client‑side authority → Speed‑hack, teleport, infinite health. |
| **Database** | Over‑exposed MongoDB (no auth), default admin user, insecure network exposure. |
| **DoS** | No request throttling → cheap amplification attacks. |
| **Data leakage** | Sending full player objects (including internal IDs) to every client. |

These points can guide a **security‑research** or **bug‑bounty** engagement.

