It uses plain JavaScript and the HTML5 `<canvas>` element, so you don’t need any external libraries.

The game is deliberately simple:

* **Player tank** – moves with **W A S D** and rotates with the mouse.  
* **Enemy tanks** – spawn at random locations and move toward the player.  
* **Bullets** – left‑mouse‑click to fire a projectile that destroys an enemy on contact.  
* **Score** – increments when an enemy is eliminated.  

Feel free to expand the code (add more enemies, obstacles, power‑ups, etc.) – the basic architecture is all there.

---

## 1. `index.html`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Mini Military Game</title>
  <style>
    body { margin:0; overflow:hidden; background:#222; color:#fff; font-family:sans-serif; }
    #ui {
      position: absolute; left: 10px; top: 10px;
      font-size: 18px; z-index: 10;
    }
    canvas { display:block; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="ui">Score: <span id="score">0</span></div>
  <canvas id="game"></canvas>

  <script src="game.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

*The `<canvas>` will fill the whole window; the UI overlay shows the current score.*

