|--------|------------|
| **Replay Attack** (reuse of old signed URL) | Set `expiresIn` to a low value (≤ 15 min) and reject any `uploadId` not present in your temporary store. |
| **Unauthorized user** | Authenticate every request (JWT, session cookie). Include the user ID in the metadata you store with `uploadId` and verify on `complete`. |
| **Man‑in‑the‑middle on pre‑signed URLs** | All traffic must be over TLS (`https`). Browsers enforce it automatically for `fetch`. |
| **Storing bucket‐wide credentials** | Use **IAM role attached to the EC2/ECS task**; no static keys in the code. |
| **DoS via massive partCount** | Enforce a max `partCount` (e.g., 10 000) and minimal `partSize` (≥ 5 MiB per S3 spec). |

