| No `return` after `ApiError.forbidden(...)` | Execution continues, `res` is never sent → the client hangs. | `return ApiError.forbidden('Нет доступа');` |
| `catch` block discards the original error | You lose the stack trace, making debugging harder. | `catch (err) { console.error(err); return ApiError.internal('…'); }` |
| Missing `await` on `avatar.mv(...)` / `background.mv(...)` (the library returns a **promise** when you don’t pass a callback) | Files may not be written before you update the DB, leading to stale paths. | `await avatar.mv(...);` (or use the callback version). |

Fixing those issues makes the upload path reachable, after which you can focus on **hardening** the endpoint (validation, path‑traversal protection, etc.).

