npm i uuid express-fileupload

# 2️⃣ Ensure uploads folder exists and is writeable
mkdir -p uploads && chmod 750 uploads

# 3️⃣ Add middleware (order matters!)
app.use(require('express-fileupload')({
  limits: { fileSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024 }, // 5 MiB
  abortOnLimit: true,
  safeFileNames: true,   // optional, adds extra sanitisation
  preserveExtension: true,
}));

# 4️⃣ Replace your old controller with the cleaned‑up version above.
# 5️⃣ Test, then push to production with TLS enabled.
```

With those changes the endpoint will **actually upload files**, **return proper responses**, and be **significantly more resilient** against the most common web‑app attacks.  

Happy coding – and stay safe! 🚀

