*Why?*  
When you keep the description in a plain‑text string (or at most a single sanitized HTML fragment), you can safely inject it via `textContent` (or via a *whitelisted* `innerHTML` that you explicitly generate).  This eliminates the most common XSS vector – a malicious string that contains a `<script>` tag.

