**Why this works**  

* `IntercaptedWebSocket` *extends* the native class, so all internal state (`_url`, readyState, etc.) is exactly what the browser expects.  
* The overridden `send` method sits **on the instance**, so every call goes through the wrapper.  
* Because we replace `window.WebSocket` *before* any other script runs, **every** subsequent `new WebSocket(...)` will be an instance of our subclass – automatically intercepted.

