```

If you have no reference, you’re out of luck – browsers do not expose a global list of live WebSocket objects. The only practical way to get a hold of them is to **inject** your patch *before* they’re created (see the previous section).  

> **Tip for security research:** When you can control the *page* (e.g., via a browser extension or userscript), you can inject a `<script>` element that runs **as early as possible** (document‑start) so you capture *every* socket the page opens.

