|-------|---------------|-----|
| `return new Proxy(this, …)` inside a class constructor | The return value is ignored; `new WebSocketInterceptor()` always yields the class instance (`this`). | Use a **factory function** (not a class) that returns a Proxy, or **extend** the native class (`class InterceptedWebSocket extends OriginalWebSocket`). |
| You never assign the proxy back to `window.WebSocket` | All later `new WebSocket(...)` calls still hit the native constructor, not your interceptor. | After defining the proxy/factory, do `window.WebSocket = WebSocketInterceptor;` (or `window.WebSocket = InterceptedWebSocket`). |
| Only wrapping new connections | Existing sockets stay untouched. | Either (a) patch each known instance manually, or (b) inject your code **before** anyone creates a socket. |
| Binary payloads (`ArrayBuffer`, `Blob`) not handled | `console.log` prints `[object ArrayBuffer]` and you may unintentionally corrupt data if you treat it as a string. | Detect the type (`if (data instanceof ArrayBuffer) …`) and decode/encode appropriately (e.g., using `TextDecoder`). |
