## 1️⃣ Adding Filtering to a Grid – “the how”

> **What you need to tell me** – a short note on the exact grid you are using (e.g. AG‑Grid, DataTables, Kendo UI, Syncfusion, plain HTML table, etc.) and the front‑end framework (React, Angular, Vue, plain JavaScript).  
> The snippets below are written for **plain JavaScript/HTML** and **React + AG‑Grid** because those are the most frequently requested. If you’re on a different stack, let me know and I’ll adapt the code.

Below are three patterns that work for *any* data‑grid library:

| Feature | What it does | Where the code lives |
|---------|--------------|----------------------|
| **Column filter UI** | Small input (or dropdown) per column header that narrows the rows based on that column only | Inside the column definition (or a header‑template) |
| **Global search box** | One text input that filters on *any* column | At the top of the page (outside the grid) |
| **Debounce + sanitisation** | Prevents “too many requests” and stops injection attacks (SQL/NoSQL/DOM) | Wrapper around the input events |

---

### 1A – Plain JavaScript / HTML Table

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Filterable Table</title>
  <style>
    th, td { padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #ddd; }
    th input { width: 90%; }
    .search-box { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="search-box">
  <label> Global search:
    <input type="text" id="globalSearch" placeholder="type to filter…">
  </label>
</div>

<table id="myTable">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Id <input type="text" data-col="0" class="col-filter" placeholder="filter…"></th>
      <th>Name <input type="text" data-col="1" class="col-filter" placeholder="filter…"></th>
      <th>Role <input type="text" data-col="2" class="col-filter" placeholder="filter…"></th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Id</th><th>Name</th><th>Role</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <!-- rows go here, generated by backend or static -->
    <tr><td>1</td><td>Alice</td><td>Admin</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Bob</td><td>User</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Charlie</td><td>Guest</td></tr>
    <!-- … -->
  </tbody>
</table>

<script>
/* ---------- Helper: simple debounce (300 ms) ---------- */
function debounce(fn, wait) {
  let timeout;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(timeout);
    timeout = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), wait);
  };
}

/* ---------- Core filter logic ---------- */
function filterTable() {
  const table = document.getElementById('myTable');
  const rows = [...table.tBodies[0].rows];
  const global = document.getElementById('globalSearch').value.trim().toLowerCase();

  // Build an array of per‑column filter strings
  const colFilters = [...document.querySelectorAll('.col-filter')].map(input => ({
    idx: parseInt(input.dataset.col, 10),
    txt: input.value.trim().toLowerCase()
  }));

  rows.forEach(row => {
    const cells = [...row.cells];
    let visible = true;

    // ----- Global filter (any column) -----
    if (global) {
      const matchesGlobal = cells.some(td => td.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(global));
      if (!matchesGlobal) visible = false;
    }

    // ----- Per‑column filters -----
    for (const {idx, txt} of colFilters) {
      if (txt && !cells[idx].textContent.toLowerCase().includes(txt)) {
        visible = false;
        break;
      }
    }

    row.style.display = visible ? '' : 'none';
  });
}

/* ---------- Wire events (debounced) ---------- */
document.getElementById('globalSearch').addEventListener('input', debounce(filterTable, 300));
document.querySelectorAll('.col-filter').forEach(inp =>
  inp.addEventListener('input', debounce(filterTable, 300))
);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**What you get**

* A **global search** box at the top that searches every column.  
* An **input field in each header** that filters only that column.  
* **Debounce (300 ms)** to keep the UI responsive and limit how often the script runs.  

---

### 1B – React + AG‑Grid (the “enterprise” grid)

