## 1. Quick “why it blows up” checklist  

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix (quick) |
|---------|--------------|-------------|
| **`Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'checked' of null`** | One (or both) of the radio inputs (`#red` / `#blue`) is not present in the DOM when `handleBetClick()` runs. | Verify the markup exists *before* you call the function (or guard with `if (redRadio && blueRadio) …`). |
| **`Uncaught ReferenceError: purse is not defined`** | `purse` is used as a global but never declared. | Declare it (`let purse = 100;`) or pass it as an argument. |
| **Double semicolon (`+ purse;;`)** | Harmless, but a typo that can mask other errors. | Remove the extra `;`. |
| **`parentDiv.innerHTML = …`** | `innerHTML` will **replace** the whole `#results` element, destroying the radio‑button set you just queried. | Use `textContent` for plain text or a dedicated child `<div>` for the status message, leaving the original controls intact. |
| **`setAttribute('onclick', 'handleButtonClick()')`** | Inline string‑based handler is evaluated via `Function` under the hood – a **DOM‑based XSS** surface if any part of the string ever contains user‑controlled data. | Use `addEventListener('click', handleButtonClick)` instead. |

---

## 2. Why “event delegation” is a good idea here  

If the radio buttons are dynamically added or removed (e.g. after betting), attaching a listener directly to each `<input type="radio">` can become brittle. A single listener on a **stable ancestor** (the form, the results container, or `document`) can:

1. **Capture clicks** on any radio that may appear later.  
2. **Avoid re‑binding** after you replace the DOM (which you currently do when you call `parentDiv.innerHTML = …`).  
3. **Reduce the attack surface** – you only expose one listener instead of many scattered `onclick` attributes.

### Minimal, secure delegation example  

```html
<div id="betting">
  <label for="red"><input type="radio" name="color" id="red" value="red">Red</label>
  <label for="blue"><input type="radio" name="color" id="blue" value="blue">Blue</label>
  <button id="betBtn">Place Bet</button>
  <div id="results"></div>
</div>
```

```js
// ---------- Global state ----------
let purse = 100;      // example starting balance

// ---------- Helper: safe DOM insertion ----------
function setStatus(msg) {
  const status = document.createElement('p');
  status.textContent = msg;               // <-- no HTML parsing
  const results = document.getElementById('results');
  results.innerHTML = '';                 // clear previous status/buttons
  results.appendChild(status);
}

// ---------- Central event hub ----------
document.getElementById('betting').addEventListener('click', e => {
  const target = e.target;

  // --- Radio button clicks (delegated) ---
  if (target.matches('input[name="color"]')) {
    // Optionally give immediate visual feedback
    console.log('Radio changed to', target.value);
    return;
  }

  // --- Place‑bet button ---
  if (target.id === 'betBtn') {
    handleBetClick();
    return;
  }

  // --- Dynamically created Start‑Race button (delegated) ---
  if (target.id === 'startRaceBtn') {
    handleButtonClick(); // your race logic
    return;
  }
});
```

```js
function handleBetClick() {
  // 1️⃣ Guard against missing radios (defensive)
  const redRadio = document.getElementById('red');
  const blueRadio = document.getElementById('blue');

  if (!redRadio || !blueRadio) {
    setStatus('Radio buttons are missing – cannot place bet.');
    return;
  }

  // 2️⃣ Determine selection safely
  let chosenColor = '';
  if (redRadio.checked) {
    chosenColor = 'red';
  } else if (blueRadio.checked) {
    chosenColor = 'blue';
  }

  // 3️⃣ Update purse – guard against under‑flow
  const betAmount = 5;
  if (purse < betAmount) {
    setStatus('Insufficient funds.');
    return;
  }
  purse -= betAmount;

  // 4️⃣ Render status + Start‑Race button (no innerHTML)
  const results = document.getElementById('results');

  if (chosenColor) {
    setStatus(`You bet on ${chosenColor} $${betAmount}. Balance: $${purse}`);
  } else {
    setStatus('Please choose a color to bet on.');
    // Bail out early – no start button if they didn’t pick
    return;
  }

  // 5️⃣ Append a *real* button with an event listener (no inline JS)
  const startBtn = document.createElement('button');
  startBtn.id = 'startRaceBtn';
  startBtn.textContent = 'Start Race';
  results.appendChild(startBtn);
}
