* Takes a **cost price** and either a **percentage markup** **or** a **fixed amount markup**.  
* Calculates the **selling price**, **gross profit**, and **gross margin**.  
* Shows the results in a **dynamic Chart.js bar chart** (you can also switch to a line chart with one click).  
* Is written with **security‑first practices** in mind – no inline `eval`, strict CSP‑friendly, sanitised inputs, and a minimal attack surface.

---  

## 1️⃣  Security‑by‑Design Checklist  

| ✅ | Topic | What we did |
|---|-------|--------------|
| **1** | **Content‑Security‑Policy (CSP)** | All scripts and styles are loaded from trusted CDNs (`self` + `cdnjs.cloudflare.com`). Inline `<style>` and `<script>` are avoided – the example uses separate files, but you can inline them if you add the proper `nonce`/`hash` to the CSP header. |
| **2** | **Strict mode & ES‑modules** | JavaScript runs in `'use strict';` and is bundled as an ES‑module, preventing accidental globals. |
| **3** | **Input validation / sanitisation** | All numeric fields are parsed with `Number()` and verified with `Number.isFinite`. Empty or non‑numeric values are rejected before any calculation. |
| **4** | **No `eval` / `Function` constructors** | The calculator never executes code from user input. |
| **5** | **HTTPS / Subresource Integrity (SRI)** | The external libraries (Chart.js & Bootstrap) are loaded over HTTPS with SRI hashes, guaranteeing the code you receive is exactly the one you expect. |
| **6** | **XSS mitigation** | The only values injected into the DOM are numbers (converted by `toLocaleString`) – no raw HTML strings are ever written. |
| **7** | **Same‑origin policy & CORS** | The page does not request any cross‑origin resources beyond the static CDNs, so there is no opportunity for CORS‑based data leakage. |
| **8** | **Secure headers (for production)** | When you host this page, add at least: `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, and `Feature-Policy: camera 'none'; microphone 'none'`. |
| **9** | **Audit‑ready** | All external dependencies have locked versions, making reproducing the exact environment trivial. |

