Below is a **complete, end‑to‑end recipe** that you can follow to add a **declarative List Action** (the ribbon button that appears on a view) which:

1. **Shows a popup** (an HTML Web‑Resource rendered as a modal dialog).  
2. Lets the user **pick a file** (drag‑and‑drop or browse).  
3. When the user clicks **Submit**, the file is uploaded as an **Annotation (Document)** and **attached to every record that was selected in the grid**.  

The solution is built **entirely with declarative customizations** (Ribbon Workbench, a custom Action, a Dialog Web‑Resource and a few JavaScript functions). No plug‑ins or server‑side code are required – everything talks to the **Dynamics 365 Web API**.

---

## 1. High‑level Architecture

| Component | What it does | Where it lives |
|-----------|--------------|----------------|
| **List Action (Ribbon button)** | Appears on the view toolbar, enabled only when at least one row is selected. Calls a JavaScript command. | Ribbon Workbench (or solution XML) |
| **JavaScript command** | • Reads the selected rows (GUIDs) • Opens the HTML dialog (`Xrm.Navigation.openWebResource`). | Web‑Resource (JS) |
| **HTML Dialog Web‑Resource** | UI: file picker, optional description, **Submit** / **Cancel** buttons. | Web‑Resource (HTML + CSS + JS) |
| **Dialog JS** | • Reads the file → Base‑64 string • Calls the **Web API** to create an `annotation` record for **each selected record** • Shows progress / success message → Closes dialog. | Embedded in the HTML Web‑Resource |
| **Web API** | `POST /api/data/v9.2/annotations` – creates an Annotation (Document) with `objectid` = target record ID. | Cloud (no code to deploy) |

> **Why use the Web‑API instead of a plug‑in?**  
> • Works in both classic & Unified Interface.  
> • No need for a sandbox plug‑in (you avoid deployment & versioning headaches).  
> • The same code can be reused in Power Automate later, if you choose that route.

---

## 2. Prerequisites

| Item | Minimum version |
|------|-----------------|
| **Dynamics 365 / Power Apps** | v9.0 (Web API v9.x) |
| **User role** | Must have **Create** permission on the **Annotation (Notes)** entity and **Read** permission on the target entity (e.g., `account`, `contact`, custom entity). |
| **Solution** | Create a new unmanaged solution (or use an existing one) – keep everything tidy. |
| **Tools** | *Ribbon Workbench* (XrmToolBox) – to add the List Action. Any text editor/IDE for the JS/HTML. |

