## 3️⃣ Security Checklist (what you should still verify)

| Category | Recommendation |
|----------|----------------|
| **Transport encryption** | Deploy TLS certificates and use the `wss://` scheme in production. Docker/K8s can terminate TLS at an ingress (NGINX, Traefik, ALB…) and forward as plain WS to the backend. |
| **Authentication & Authorization** | Right now *any* client can join.  In a real product you’d add a short‑lived JWT (issued by an auth service) and verify it in `verifyClient`. |
| **Origin‑checking** | Already enforced via `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`.  Keep the list as narrow as possible. |
| **Input validation** | Server sanitises text, but you may also want to whitelist allowed characters (e.g., no control chars). |
| **File type controls** | If you only need images, check `file.type.startsWith('image/')` on both client and server before forwarding. |
| **Rate‑limiting & DoS protection** | Token bucket per socket helps, but consider a **global request‑rate** bucket (e.g., using `express-rate-limit`) and a reverse‑proxy (NGINX, Cloudflare) that can throttle at the network layer. |
| **Logging & monitoring** | Ship `pino` logs to a centralized system and set alerts on spikes in connection failures, high error rates, or abnormal message sizes. |
| **Graceful shutdown** | On SIGTERM/SIGINT, close the HTTP server, stop accepting new WS connections, and give existing sockets a short timeout to finish. |
| **Dependency hygiene** | Keep `ws`, `express`, `helmet`, etc. up‑to‑date. Run `npm audit` regularly and consider `npm audit fix` or `snyk` for CI checks. |
| **Content‑Security‑Policy (CSP)** | Even though we only use a textarea, adding a strict CSP (e.g., `default-src 'self'`) prevents accidental script injection if the page ever expands. |
| **CORS** | The server currently uses `cors()` with defaults (allows all origins). In production restrict it to the exact domain(s) that host the chat UI. |

