|------|--------|------------|
| **Request method** | CSRF (cross‑site request forgery) | CSRF token verification (`verify_csrf_token`). |
| **Operator whitelist** | Command injection / arbitrary code execution | Only a static set `['+','-','*','/','^','sqrt']` is accepted. |
| **Number validation** | Injection via non‑numeric strings (`"1; rm -rf /"` etc.) | `filter_var(..., FILTER_VALIDATE_FLOAT)` forces a float. |
| **Division by zero / root‑index zero** | Application error/exceptions → information leakage | Explicit checks with custom error handling. |
| **Arithmetic performed in PHP** | No `eval()` or user‑controlled functions. |
| **Error handling** | Stack‑trace disclosure | Errors logged to server log only (`error_log`). |
| **PRG (Post‑Redirect‑Get)** | Duplicate submissions, accidental re‑calculations (Refresh). |
| **Result encoding** | Reflected XSS via `?result=` | `rawurlencode` when building redirect URL, and `htmlspecialchars` when echoing on the page. |
| **Session usage** | Session fixation | `session_start()` at the top of each script, and you can add `session_regenerate_id(true)` after login if you extend the app. |
| **Headers** (optional) | Click‑jacking, MIME sniffing | You can add security headers in an `.htaccess` or PHP snippet (`Header::set`). |

