## 7. Scheduling with Cron  

Add the following entry to the `dbbackup` user’s crontab (`crontab -e`):

```
# Daily backup at 02:10 AM, redirect stdout/stderr to syslog via logger
10 2 * * * /usr/bin/php /home/dbbackup/backup_mysql.php >> /var/log/dbbackup.log 2>&1
```

*Tip:* If you prefer **systemd timers**, you can wrap the same command in a short service unit.  

---

## 8. Verifying the Backup (post‑run)

```bash
# List recent backups (encrypted)
ls -lh /var/backups/mysql/*.gpg

# Decrypt a sample (on a workstation with the private key)
gpg --output - --decrypt /var/backups/mysql/all_2024-03-15_02-10-00.sql.gz.gpg | gzip -d | head -n 20
